+                          # UNDER_NARROW_Z. It REPLACES the front tuck rather
+                          # than stacking on it (see hem_rake) - below the raked
+                          # hem there is no outer shell left to stay parallel to,
+                          # so the "hold them UNDER_INSET apart" rule has nothing
